==Swedish==
{{sv-verb-irreg|bära|bär|bar|burit|bär|bärande|buren}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmq-osw|sv}} ''[[bæra]]'' ({{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|bera|lang=non}}).
Cognate with Danish {{term|bære|lang=da}} and Norwegian {{term|bære|lang=no}}. <ref>{{cite web |last=Hellquist |first=Elof |authorlink= |coauthors= | date= |url=http://runeberg.org/svetym/0166.html |title=Svensk etymologisk ordbok |format= |work= |pages= |publisher= | language=Swedish |accessdate=2009-06-09 |accessyear= }}</ref>

See the English verb {{term|bear|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-bära.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
'''bära'''

# [[carry]]; to lift and transport anywhere else
# [[wear]]; e.g. a piece of clothing or jewelery
# (''somewhat dated'') [[lead]] to; end up at

====Related terms====
;lead to
* [[alla vägar bär till Rom]]

====Synonyms====
;lead to
* [[leda]] (till)

